  2609	## D204 · 2026-10-28 · A repeat is stored as its own source record; the merge becomes a labelled relation
  2610	
  2611	- Alex: "补那个洞，跑一周验收，仔细思考很重要". The hole (D203's census): on a `repeat` decision the writer adds the incoming item as an outlet of the old piece and discards the incoming text; 8 of 40 sampled repeats (20%, about 200 of 1,034 in the run) had merged a different or richer statement, and its content was gone. The mechanism is D202's: a one-draw label (same_statement ≥ 0.5) triggers an irreversible write.
  2612	- Choice weighed. (A) Store the incoming piece, link it to its own destinations, record the pair in `same_claims`, show both to the judge with the relation labelled as the matcher's opinion. (B) Keep the merge and store the text as a variant of the old piece, hidden from the judge. Under (A) true pickups (about 80%) appear twice in view for their first readings, labelled; under (B) the 20% wrong merges stay hidden from the judge. The standard (rule A: an outlet, not a fact; rule C: support counts sources) is served by the label; losing content is the failure that is not recoverable at read time. Decided: (A).
  2613	- Decided: `writing` stores every incoming piece once with all its destination links; a `repeat` decision records (target, new, seq) in `same_claims`; the old piece gains no source row and no new link (the new piece carries the outlet and the links; a link written on a one-draw label is a write like any other). `store.evidence_in_force` carries `same_as` (the in-force pieces of its group); the judge's request prints "Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as eX; the argument counts one claim". Readers of `evidence`, `evidence_links` and `evidence_sources` keep their shapes; the library UI's per-row outlet count now counts one row's sources (the claim's outlets are its `same_claims` group), an open UI item.
  2614	- Acceptance: tests red on the old writer (`test_a_repeated_statement_is_stored_as_its_own_record…`, the two D167 tests whose assertions pinned the merge, changed with this decision), a mutant that merges again fails them; the 40 sampled repeat decisions replayed through the new writer at $0 (40/40 stored, relation recorded, the 8 lost contents present); then one week through the whole path (`english-v34c-nvda-week`), counting `same_claims` rows, pairs both in the judge's view, and judgements citing both members of a pair (the double-count exposure the label must hold).
  2615	- Accepted ([results](research/2026-10-27-stage34-gold/results.md)): 40 of 40 sampled repeat decisions replayed through the new writer keep the piece, the relation and both pieces in force (the 8 lost contents are present); the week through the whole path ran with none failed at $0.23, wrote 45 same-claim relations and no merge, and the judge's reasons where a pair was in view treat the relays as one source ("ultimately trace to SemiAnalysis", "not independent confirmation"). The three-month run may resume on `poc-v34` with D202–D204 in the writer; that is Alex's call.
